# SurfCPU: SHA-256 of the generated LiteDRAM files the DDR designs build from (paths relative
# to surfcpu/, sha256sum format). File: arty.sha256, written by ip/litedram/lock.sh write.
# generate: make litedram-gen
# ip/litedram/generate.sh makes them byte for byte the same on every run and in every checkout
# (make litedram-repro), in the toolchain
# image surfcpu-toolchain:2026-10-15, from the generator ip/litedram/setup.sh pins,
# ip/litedram/arty.yml and SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH 1790239353 (the LiteDRAM commit's
# time). tools/fpga-build.sh and make litedram-gen check them (ip/litedram/lock.sh check).
# csr.csv and sdram_phy.h are the register map and the PHY settings the firmware's DDR
# initialization was written for (make litedram-gen compares them with spec/soc.toml and
# firmware/common/ddrinit_phy.h). The last line is the simulation core (make
# test-ddr-litedram, make board-ddr-sim), not part of any bitstream.
